<item>
            <title>[LU-20894] Build fails against kernels without CONFIG_XARRAY_MULTI set</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20894</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19179&quot; title=&quot;Remove 3.10 kernel support (rhel/rocky/centos7)&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19179&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19179&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; removed RHEL 7 kernel support and along with it, removed the copy of XArray from the Lustre tree and relied on the in-kernel XArray implementation. It also added a configure test that checks for the presence of CONFIG_XARRAY_MULTI, so that the build fails, just in case Lustre is built against a kernel without XArray support.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;CONFIG_XARRAY_MULTI doesn&apos;t denote core XArray support, though, but the presence of an XArray feature for supporting entries, which occupy multiple consecutive indices in the XArray; it was assumed that CONFIG_XARRAY_MULTI would normally always be set, as CONFIG_ZONE_DEVICE, which is also expected to be normally set (and also CONFIG_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE) select CONFIG_XARRAY_MULTI. It seems to be possible in practice, to not have either of these configuration options set in some SLES 15 SP2/SP3 kernels (probably with a custom configuration) that we have built against and this should also be possible on kernels of any currently supported distributions and on vanilla kernels.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The functionality provided by CONFIG_XARRAY_MULTI isn&apos;t used by Lustre and core XArray support should be sufficient, so this shouldn&apos;t be a requirement. We could reinstate the previous configure check that verified the presence of XArray via a compilation test, to address this issue.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
